The table structure information is (table names): 
['hardware_dim_customer', 'hardware_fact_pre_invoice_deductions', 'web_sales_reps', 'hardware_dim_product', 'web_orders', 'StaffHours', 'university_enrollment', 'university_faculty', 'university_student', 'university_offering', 'web_accounts', 'web_events', 'SalaryDataset', 'web_region', 'hardware_fact_gross_price', 'hardware_fact_manufacturing_cost', 'university_course', 'hardware_fact_sales_monthly']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

hardware_fact_sales_monthly  
• date – filter records to the calendar year 2021.  
• product_code – link every sales record to its product master data.  
• sold_quantity – quantity metric to be aggregated.  

hardware_dim_product  
• product_code – join field to the fact table.  
• division – required to slice the results “in each division”.  

(Only those two tables are needed for the requested KPI.)

Below are ten exploratory ‑> incremental SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that move from very simple inspection to the final logic that yields the requested answer.  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at raw 2021 sales records (first 20 rows).
SELECT *
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly
WHERE strftime('%Y', date) = '2021'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct months represented in calendar‑year 2021.
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y‑%m', date) AS month_2021
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly
WHERE strftime('%Y', date) = '2021'
ORDER BY month_2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Total quantity sold per product during 2021 (top 20 by volume).
SELECT product_code,
       SUM(sold_quantity) AS total_qty_2021
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly
WHERE strftime('%Y', date) = '2021'
GROUP BY product_code
ORDER BY total_qty_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join products to see which divisions the 20 best‑selling
-- products (overall) belong to.
SELECT s.product_code,
       p.division,
       SUM(s.sold_quantity) AS total_qty_2021
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
JOIN hardware_dim_product    AS p
  ON s.product_code = p.product_code
WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
GROUP BY s.product_code, p.division
ORDER BY total_qty_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: For one division sample (e.g., 'P & A'), list products by volume.
SELECT p.division,
       s.product_code,
       SUM(s.sold_quantity) AS total_qty_2021
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
  ON s.product_code = p.product_code
WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
  AND p.division = 'P & A'
GROUP BY p.division, s.product_code
ORDER BY total_qty_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Rank products inside each division by 2021 volume
-- and keep only the top 3 (window function).
SELECT division,
       product_code,
       total_qty_2021,
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY division ORDER BY total_qty_2021 DESC) AS rnk
FROM (
    SELECT p.division,
           s.product_code,
           SUM(s.sold_quantity) AS total_qty_2021
    FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
    JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
      ON s.product_code = p.product_code
    WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
    GROUP BY p.division, s.product_code
) AS t
WHERE rnk <= 3
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Average monthly quantity for every product in 2021
-- (shows that we can also average over rows, not needed but exploratory).
SELECT p.division,
       s.product_code,
       AVG(s.sold_quantity) AS avg_monthly_qty
FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
  ON s.product_code = p.product_code
WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
GROUP BY p.division, s.product_code
ORDER BY avg_monthly_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Bring the top‑3 per division (CTE) and compute
-- their grand‑total quantity in 2021.
WITH top3 AS (
    SELECT division,
           product_code,
           SUM(sold_quantity) AS total_qty,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY division ORDER BY SUM(sold_quantity) DESC) AS rnk
    FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
    JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
      ON s.product_code = p.product_code
    WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
    GROUP BY division, product_code
)
SELECT division,
       SUM(total_qty) AS qty_of_top3
FROM top3
WHERE rnk <= 3
GROUP BY division
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same top‑3 CTE but now compute the overall *average*
-- quantity sold across those three products (per division).
WITH top3 AS (
    SELECT division,
           product_code,
           SUM(sold_quantity) AS total_qty,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY division ORDER BY SUM(sold_quantity) DESC) AS rnk
    FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
    JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
      ON s.product_code = p.product_code
    WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
    GROUP BY division, product_code
)
SELECT division,
       AVG(total_qty) AS avg_qty_top3_products_2021
FROM top3
WHERE rnk <= 3
GROUP BY division
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description (final answer query): For calendar‑year 2021, return
-- the overall average quantity sold of the top three best‑selling
-- hardware products (by total quantity) in each division.
WITH ranked_products AS (
    SELECT p.division,
           s.product_code,
           SUM(s.sold_quantity) AS total_qty_2021,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY p.division
               ORDER BY SUM(s.sold_quantity) DESC
           ) AS rnk
    FROM hardware_fact_sales_monthly AS s
    JOIN hardware_dim_product AS p
      ON s.product_code = p.product_code
    WHERE strftime('%Y', s.date) = '2021'
    GROUP BY p.division, s.product_code
)
SELECT division,
       ROUND(AVG(total_qty_2021), 2) AS avg_qty_top3_products_2021
FROM ranked_products
WHERE rnk <= 3
GROUP BY division
LIMIT 20;
```
